+
+## Open-room membership (opt-in)
+
+Humans still auto-join every open room (`User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms`
++ `Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users`). Bots no longer do.
+
+Bots opt in via `users.join_open_rooms` (`boolean`, default `false`), exposed
+in the bot form (new + edit) as a real checkbox styled as a switch with the
+visible label "Add to all open rooms" (off by default).
+`BotsController#bot_params` permits `:join_open_rooms`.
+
+- `User.joining_open_rooms` = `humans.or(bots.where(join_open_rooms: true))`;
+  `Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users` grants to
+  `User.active.joining_open_rooms`, so new/converted open rooms pick up
+  humans + opted-in bots only.
+- `User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms` returns early for bots without the
+  flag; bots created with the flag on join all existing opens.
+- `User#join_all_open_rooms` (+ `after_update_commit
+  :join_all_open_rooms_if_enabled` when `join_open_rooms` flips `false→true`)
+  inserts the missing open memberships. Turning the flag off keeps current
+  memberships (no-op).
+- All membership writes go through `Room#memberships.grant_to` (also used by
+  `Room.create_for` and `revise`), which diffs against existing memberships
+  (`insert_all` ignores duplicates on SQLite, but we diff explicitly so
+  `joined` fires exactly once) and then calls `Room#notify_bots_joined`.
+
+## Webhooks (`joined` event)
+
+Whenever a bot gains a non-direct membership — automatically (flag on at
+create, flag turned on, new/converted open room) or by a person (closed-room
+`revise`/`create_for`) — we enqueue exactly one
+`BotWebhookJob.perform_later(nil, bot.id, room.id)` per newly-added bot via
+`Room#notify_bots_joined` / `User#join_all_open_rooms` /
+`User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms`. Direct rooms never trigger `joined`.
+Only bots with `webhook_url` present are enqueued; the job re-checks
+`room.direct?`, `webhook_url.blank?` and `bot.active?`.
+
+`BotJoinedPayload#to_h` builds:
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "joined",
+  "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/<bot_token>/messages" }
+}
+```
+
+`reply_to` matches the `mention` payload format
+(`/rooms/:room_id/:bot_token/messages`).
+
+`BotWebhookJob#perform(message_id, bot_id, room_id = nil)` dispatches:
+`message_id` present → `mention` (`BotWebhookPayload`), `message_id=nil` +
+`room_id` present → `joined` (`BotJoinedPayload`). `POST` + reply handling
+(`204` nothing; `200` `text/plain`/`text/html` non-blank →
+`room.messages.create_with_attachment!(creator: bot, ...)` +
+`broadcast_create`; else ignored; never raises) is shared, so `joined`
+replies post the same way as `mention` replies.
